Spoilers, I suppose.




Use that athame! Everytime you get into trouble, engrave Elbereth. Athame's
don't get dull when engraving unless they're cursed. My last wizard game, I
forgot I had a ring of searching on and went into a huge shop full of mimics.
I collected everything in the shop, engraving at every step, and then teleported
out with tons of scrolls, potions, and a wand of wishing!

Never get into HtH unless you have full hit points. Do the levels as fast as you
can until you get a couple of food rations. Keep your pet as long as possible. 
Keep all the scrolls and potions you run into, even the bad ones. Fight with
your athame until you run into tough monsters ( >15 hp ). Throw stuff.

As for the mines, I'll do the first couple of levels using hit and run tactics
to pick up a pickaxe and dwarven chain, and then keep heading down the dungeon
proper until I at least hit the oracle level. If I find things are going well
by then, I go back to the mines. You generally have enough money by then (from
raiding vaults with that pickaxe) to make the town level work for you.

God, I sound like a self-help manual.

